nothing here grants a permission the Elastic License 2.0 withholds.

## 1. No hosting, no managed service

The limitation in the "Limitations" section of the Elastic License 2.0 is not limited to
public clouds. You may not provide the software to any third party as a hosted, managed,
co-branded, embedded-in-a-service, or otherwise remotely accessible offering, whether paid
or free, whether to customers, affiliates, or the public, when that offering gives its
users access to a substantial set of the features or functionality of the software. This
includes operating the daemon on someone else's behalf and reaching their stores with it.

Running the software for your own organisation's own stores, on infrastructure you control,
is permitted and needs no contract.

## 2. Marks and attribution

The name "Okto", "Okto Labs", "Okto Grafx", and the octagonal graph mark are trademarks of
Okto Labs. If you distribute the software, or a copy of it, unmodified, you must keep the
name, the mark and the attribution in the operator console, in this notice, and in the
license file intact.

If you modify the software in a way you would describe as more than a bug fix or a local
configuration change, remove the Okto Grafx mark and the console's branding, and rename
your work so that it is not presented as Okto Grafx. Nothing in this license is a licence
to the marks themselves.

## 3. No endorsement

Nothing in this license permits you to state or imply that Okto Labs endorses, sponsors,
or supports you, your deployment, or a modified version of the software.

## 4. Distributions and builds

Any copy you distribute must carry this file, unmodified, including the notices in the
Elastic License 2.0 text above. If you distribute a build of the operator console, the
